# patch: 008-idle-signal-chunked
# format: CHUNKED ONLY (2.1.242+). Monolithic keeps 008-idle-signal.patch.
# version: authored against 2.1.260
# depends: 002
# description: Emits {type:"idle"} when the REPL is at rest. The orchestrator
#              keys on this to know a seat is free.
#
# 🔴 REDUCED IN SCOPE ON PURPOSE — READ BEFORE RELYING ON IT.
#   The 2.1.238 patch installed its OWN useEffect with a 400 ms settle timer and
#   a three-part rest test: `_h !== 'waiting' && !mi && z.getMainThreadQueueLength() === 0`.
#   None of those three locals is addressable on a chunked tree: the REPL body is
#   React-Compiler output (`if (Vi[230] !== TDt || Vi[231] !== LDt)` …), where
#   every local is a minified name held in a numbered memo-cache slot and adding
#   a hook that reads three of them would be exactly the silent-misbinding hazard
#   the patch rules forbid.
#
#   So this emits from INSIDE the existing session-activity effect instead, whose
#   callback already receives the REPL's own computed status:
#       l$e({ status: uie, waitingFor: ZHe }, JHe)
#   and fires when `uie === 'idle'` with no `waitingFor`. That is upstream's own
#   idea of idle, not a reconstruction of it.
#
#   DIFFERENCES FROM THE MONOLITHIC BEHAVIOUR, stated rather than glossed:
#     - NO 400 ms debounce. The signal fires on the status transition, so a
#       consumer that expects the settle delay may see it marginally earlier.
#     - The message-queue depth is NOT consulted. If upstream reports 'idle'
#       while a queued prompt is pending, this would emit where the old one
#       would not.
#   Both are behaviour changes in the emit CONDITION, not in the message shape;
#   {type:"idle"} is unchanged, so the orchestrator contract holds.
#
# ANCHOR: `l$e` and `uie` are minified and appear as CONTEXT (the added lines
#   reference `uie`/`ZHe`, which the context line directly above binds and gives
#   meaning to via the literal property names `status:` and `waitingFor:` —
#   those property names are the real anchor and cannot be minified).
#   `uie === 'idle'` compares against a STRING LITERAL.
#
# ⚠️ NOT EXERCISED BY THE HEADLESS TURN TEST (no REPL). Applying and bundling are
#   VERIFIED; live idle emission is BELIEVED.
#
# ============================================================================
# RE-AUTHORED 2026-09-07 — RE-CONTEXTED TO 2.1.263
# ============================================================================
# STATUS: 🔴 VERSION-LOCKED. Applies to 2.1.263 (verified); FAILS on 2.1.260
#         (verified). Not fixable without an anchor; blocking symbols named.
#
# WHAT BLOCKS IT:
#   The guard needs the CURRENT status value and the waiting-for value, and
#   both are React-compiler-memoized locals destructured from an anonymous
#   memo slot. Every identifier at the site churns:
#       2.1.260:  l$e({ status: uie, waitingFor: ZHe }, JHe).catch(aPo)
#       2.1.263:  xUe({ status: uce, waitingFor: eGe }, ZVe).catch(oFo)
#   The added line MUST read `uce`/`eGe` (the .263 spelling) because it tests
#   their values. There is no stable alias: they come from
#       let { status: xD, waitingFor: eGe, working: tGe } = IOo;
#   where `IOo` is itself a memo-cache slot (`cx[15]`), not a named export.
#
# WHY IT IS NEVERTHELESS SAFE — option (b) from the brief, applied strictly:
#   The minified names on the added line are pinned by the CONTEXT line
#   directly above them, which is the call that DEFINES their meaning:
#       xUe({ status: uce, waitingFor: eGe }, ZVe).catch(oFo);
#   That line is inside the hunk. If any of those names drift, the context
#   fails and the patch is REJECTED — it cannot apply while binding different
#   variables. Verified: this patch FAILS on 2.1.260 rather than misapplying.
#
# ⛔ WHAT WOULD UNBLOCK IT: an anchor rule naming the status-reporting call
#   (`l$e`/`xUe` — it is the "report agent status" helper) AND the destructured
#   status/waitingFor locals. Naming the helper alone is not enough; the guard
#   reads the VALUES, so the locals are what must become stable.
#
#
# 🔴 REGENERATED 2026-09-07 against the anchored tree, and the reason matters:
#   the hunk now uses replStatusForActivity / replWaitingForActivity instead of
#   the minified uce / eGe. Swapping the TOKENS was not enough — the longer
#   names made prettier REFLOW the call across three lines, so the old
#   single-line context could never match. The hunk was re-derived from the
#   real tree rather than hand-edited.
#   Note the @@ header now reads `function useReplStatusEffects(...)`: that is
#   an anchored name too, so even git's context hint is version-stable.
#
